linal (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed from Signal-L5 to Linal (package linal, app id
    io.github.andy53.Linal, command linal, services linal-daemon and
    linal-receiver). Replaces the signal-l5 package. On first start the
    app moves Signal-L5's messages, settings and logs to the new folders and
    stops its old services; signal-cli's account data is unchanged.
  * The daemon uses IPv4 only. On some mobile networks IPv6 silently drops
    large packets, which made a newly registered account hang on its first
    key upload until mobile IPv6 was turned off.
  * Removed the old standalone installer and the pre-package TCP daemon
    check.

 -- Linal Maintainers <linal@example.invalid>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0600

signal-l5 (1.0.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * One account at a time on the phone. When a different account signs in,
    or the account is logged out, everything of previous accounts is
    deleted: signal-cli's keys and data for them and its received
    attachments, and the app's messages, contacts, call log and copies of
    sent attachments. Message history is now kept per account
    (accounts/<id>/history.db).
  * "Logged out" is either Settings > Log out (new: unregisters this phone,
    then deletes) or Signal refusing the account's credentials, e.g. after
    the number was registered on another device. Being offline never
    deletes anything.

 -- Signal-L5 Maintainers <signal-l5@example.invalid>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0600

signal-l5 (1.0.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Verification code dialog: act on its first response only. Filling in the
    SMS code closed the dialog, which counted as Cancel and restarted the
    daemon in the middle of verifying; and a code sent from the keyboard or
    by auto-fill left the dialog open, so it could be sent a second time
    after registration had already succeeded.

