signal-l5 (1.0.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Local support logging: rotating logs per component in
    ~/.local/state/signal-l5/logs (private), with phone numbers, Signal IDs,
    captcha links and tokens redacted and no message text; uncaught errors are
    logged with tracebacks. Nothing is sent anywhere.
  * "Save logs for support" (main menu, Settings) writes one redacted file to
    Downloads; Settings has a "Detailed logging" switch.
  * Ask for a profile name when none is set (people otherwise see "Unknown").
  * Ring and notify once per incoming call: signal-cli reports ringing twice,
    which posted two notifications and invalidated the Answer button's token.
  * Escape notification text (Phosh renders body markup).

 -- Signal-L5 Maintainers <signal-l5@example.invalid>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0600

signal-l5 (1.0.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Registration opens the captcha in the default browser again (GNOME Web on
    PureOS) and no longer depends on firefox-esr: the HTTP 403s happened with
    captchas from Firefox too, so the browser was not the cause.
  * After a failed or abandoned registration, restart the signal-cli daemon so
    the existing account resumes receiving messages and calls (signal-cli
    closes it when a registration of the same number starts).
  * Security: the daemon serves JSON-RPC on a Unix socket in a private runtime
    directory instead of TCP 127.0.0.1:7583, which any local process (and web
    pages POSTing to localhost) could use to read messages and act as the
    account. The app restarts a pre-upgrade daemon still listening on TCP.
  * Security: discard the daemon's stdout, where signal-cli prints the text of
    every received message, so messages no longer end up in the journal.
  * Security: signall5:call links answer a call only with a one-time token
    from the incoming-call notification; other apps and web pages could
    previously answer an incoming call by opening such a link.

 -- Signal-L5 Maintainers <signal-l5@example.invalid>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 09:00:00 -0600

